{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788294818,"nonce":"5M0Qq8Rguv7ZH6E10xRwYlwjKHw=","message":"REFINEMENT FROM EVAN, VERIFIED: the divergence is a GROUND-TRADER property, and the orbital path is a different mechanism entirely. His words: \"trades happen instantly on the ground but not orbital traders, that has to get shipped.\" Both halves check out at source, and it narrows the scope of the previous comment.\n\n| | delivery |\n|---|---|\n| ground caravan (`RimWorld/Pawn_TraderTracker.GiveSoldThingToPlayer`) | `GenPlace.TryPlaceThing(thing, toGive.PositionHeld, mapHeld, ThingPlaceMode.Near)` — INSTANT, on the ground, at **the carrying caravan member's own cell** |\n| orbital (`RimWorld/TradeShip.GiveSoldThingToPlayer`) | `TradeUtility.SpawnDropPod(DropCellFinder.TradeDropSpot(map), map, thing)` -\u003e `DropPodUtility.MakeDropPodAt` — SHIPPED |\n\nSo the 69-of-80 measurement is specifically what a partially-parked CARAVAN looks like. `TradeDropSpot` searches unroofed cells beside an orbital trade beacon, falling back to any powered comms console and then to any colonist building — i.e. **it lands at the colony**, so an orbital buy very likely DOES move the deal-scoped `colony_now`.\n\nThat gives the surface a THIRD state the previous comment did not name: **a pod in flight is on neither side.** `MakeDropPodAt` spawns an `ActiveDropPod`; between `trade-confirm` returning and the pod landing, the goods are not the trader's, not `ColonyThingsWillingToBuy`, and not in `map.listerThings` as the item either. An agent that buys food orbitally and immediately reads any of the three surfaces gets \"nothing arrived\", and it is TRUE at that instant and false a few ticks later.\n\nConsequences for the fix already proposed:\n\n- The `map_now` figure must be documented as **eventually**-consistent for orbital and immediately-consistent for ground, or an orbital buy reads as a failed trade.\n- The landing-cells field is worth more, not less: for ground it is the caravan's scattered cells, for orbital it is one drop spot, and the two need different hauling answers.\n- `accept/3.5-dialog-verbs.py`'s bound (`0 \u003c= delta \u003c= line`) is correct for both — tight for orbital, loose for ground — which is the right shape for an assertion that must hold on whichever trader the fixture happens to produce. An exact assertion would have to know which path ran.\n\nEverything else in the previous comment stands.","files":null}]}